--!nocheck
-- Builds the weapon set's templates and the review showcase. Run in Studio, Edit mode, through the
-- MCP (execute_luau) or the command bar. Re-runnable: it takes its meshes from a fresh Import 3D of
-- the FBX files (art/fbx_export/) if present, otherwise from the templates already in
-- ServerStorage (WeaponModels or the staging copy), and replaces everything it built before. One
-- ChangeHistoryService recording (Ctrl+Z undoes all).
--
-- ServerStorage.WeaponModels is Rojo-managed (assets/WeaponModels.rbxm), so this builds the
-- staging copy ServerStorage._StagingWeaponModels. Export it under the real name and destroy it
-- (AGENTS.md "Studio instances"):
--   _G.exportRbxm("ServerStorage._StagingWeaponModels", "WeaponModels") -> assets/WeaponModels.rbxm
-- It holds:
--   Class weapons (Jian, Dadao, Greatsword, Guandao, Spear, Staff): a Model whose PrimaryPart is a
--     small invisible part named after the class joint (HiltR: Jian, Greatsword; Hilt: the rest),
--     attribute Joint = that name. Inside it a Motor6D of the same name: Part1 = the joint part,
--     Part0 = nil (the game sets it to the character's Right Arm), C0/C1 from the source animation
--     rigs (GreataxeRig/StaffRig/SpearRig Hilt, gsrigrea2lfixed and katanadummy HiltR), so the
--     M1 clips' Hilt/HiltR tracks drive it. The meshes are welded (WeldConstraint) to the joint
--     part, placed so that with Part0 = an R6 Right Arm in rest pose the weapon sits where the
--     source rigs hold theirs: straight forward out of the fist, the right hand on the item's
--     `grip` anchor, cutting edge down (it faces forward once the arm is raised). Every part is
--     unanchored, Massless, CanCollide/CanTouch/CanQuery false. Attachments on the joint part:
--     Tip and Base (the span a swing trail draws), plus each anchor from the bounds JSON
--     (grip, off_grip, tip, guard, ... lower case).
--   Every mesh is a Part with a FileMesh SpecialMesh (MeshId from the import, Scale fitting it to
--   the JSON size), not a MeshPart: Rojo can't set MeshPart.MeshId when it syncs the file.
--   Dizi: a Tool (main mesh = Handle, Tool.Grip from the grip anchor), Zither: a back Accessory,
--     SpiritStone: a Model with a Neon core and a PointLight (unchanged from the first pass).
--   ManualScroll: an anchored prop Model (pivot = the middle of its footprint, resting on the
--     surface) for world manual caches.
-- Workspace.WeaponShowcase: a row of clones of Workspace.Rig (real R6) holding each class weapon
--   through its Motor6D (Part0 = Right Arm), posed at the class idle's first frame, and a second
--   row in front posed at the hit frame of each class's first M1 (both sampled from the clips'
--   KeyframeSequences, written into the rig's Motor6D C0s since nothing animates in Edit mode).
--   The Dizi and Zither rigs keep their Tool hold and back carry. The source rigs that also live
--   in this folder (SpearRig, StaffRig, GreataxeRig, gsrigrea2lfixed, katanadummy, Siegfried) are
--   left alone: only Showcase_*, Posed_* and SpiritStone are replaced.
--
-- Item space ("model space"): the weapon runs along +Y (Blender +Z), Blender +X stays +X, Blender
-- +Y is -Z; the pivot is the item's build origin. Mesh sizes/centres come from the items' bounds
-- JSONs (Blender axes, studs): Size = (bx, bz, by), CFrame = pivot * Angles(0, pi, 0) *
-- CFrame.new(-cx, cz, cy). Anchors are in item space.
-- Regenerate the block below with: python3 art/weapons/gen_place_weapons.py

